#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pi-cleanup — safe, repeatable disk cleanup for git checkouts, worktrees and docker.

Usage: pi-cleanup [--apply] [--only STEPS] [--idle-days N] [--worktree-min-idle-days N]
                  [--image-age-days N] [--dev-image-age-days N]
                  [--nuget-age-days N] [--nuget-keep-versions N] [--session-age-days N] [--if-free-below GIB|config]
                  [--roots PATH ...] [--json] [--scheduled] [--budget SECONDS]

  (default)          dry run: print the plan, change nothing; use existing remote refs
  --apply            execute the plan
  --budget SECONDS   overall dry-run deadline (default 60; 0 unlimited). Unfinished
                     sections are not measured (budget), never removable. Ignored by --apply.
                     Text sections stream immediately; --json remains one complete document.
  --only STEPS       comma list of build,worktrees,docker,caches,bins (default: all five)
  --idle-days N      a repo/worktree modified within N days is ACTIVE (default 3; when
                     --scheduled and not given, only the build step uses 0.25)
  --worktree-min-idle-days N  minimum idle age for worktree removal (default 1; may be 0).
                     Effective worktree idle threshold = max(--idle-days, this value)
  --nuget-age-days N remote-sourced ~/.nuget/packages versions whose newest file
                     atime/mtime/ctime is older than N days are removed by the caches step
                     (default 7); runs even while dotnet is running
  --nuget-keep-versions N  the newest N versions of every package id are never removed
                     (default 3; at least one version always stays)
  --session-age-days N pi session .jsonl files not modified for N days are gzipped in
                     place by the caches step (default 30)
  --if-free-below GIB|config exit 0 with "free space OK" (doing nothing) when the home volume
                     and every root have at least GIB GiB free
  --image-age-days N docker images older than N days and used by no container are
                     removed with `docker rmi <id>` (default 7)
  --dev-image-age-days N unused, unpinned cratis/* images with no release tag, not named in a
                     tracked Dockerfile/compose file of any checkout, are removed per tag with
                     `docker rmi <ref>` (never -f) once their last tag is older than N days
                     (default 2); skipped, with a note, if the checkout scan fails
  --roots PATH ...   directories searched for git checkouts (default:
                     {{REPOS_ROOT}}, skipped if not mounted)
  --json             machine-readable output on stdout
  --scheduled        forces --only build,docker,caches,worktrees,bins and --apply; appends a
                     summary to ~/.pi/agent/logs/pi-cleanup.log (kept under 1 MB). Used by
                     the launchd jobs com.example.pi-cleanup (daily 03:00) and
                     com.example.pi-cleanup-lowdisk (every 30 min, with
                     --if-free-below config). If another --apply run holds the lock, a
                     scheduled run logs one line and exits 0.

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 partial (some deletions failed).

Global guard. A checkout/worktree is ACTIVE when any process has its cwd or an open
file inside it (`lsof -nP -d cwd -Fn` + `lsof -nP -Fn`, taken once and refreshed
before applying). For `build`, a checkout is also ACTIVE when the newest mtime among its
git admin files (index, HEAD, logs/HEAD) and its root dir is younger than --idle-days.
For `worktrees`, only the process guard plus idleness (below) apply. ACTIVE roots are
skipped, with the reason printed. lsof only sees this user's processes.

Steps
  build      rmtree ignored+untracked build-output dirs (bin, obj, node_modules, ...)
             in non-ACTIVE checkouts/worktrees. A dir is skipped if git tracks anything
             inside, it contains a known root or a .git entry, or a process holds a file
             in it. Never deletes a root itself. Sizes are not measured (use df).
  worktrees  remove linked worktrees that are idle >= max(--idle-days,
             --worktree-min-idle-days); idle age is that of the newest of the worktree
             git-dir's logs/HEAD and HEAD mtimes (commit/checkout/reset/rebase), so
             index rewrites by `git status` and root-dir mtime are ignored. The process
             guard stays mandatory. A worktree must also be
             clean, hold no sensitive/unknown ignored files, and whose HEAD is on
             origin/<default> after `git fetch --prune origin` of the parent (basis
             "on-default"), or is covered by a merged PR seen via gh (basis
             "merged-pr", listed separately). .ai-work is rsynced to
             <parent>/.ai-work/keep/removed-worktrees/<name>/ first. Right before
             removal: not ACTIVE, still clean, HEAD unchanged. `git worktree remove`
             is never forced; a failure stops worktree processing (exit 2).
             Dry runs never fetch: existing remote-tracking refs are used and
             reported as "remote refs not refreshed (dry run)".
  docker     container prune (24h), image prune (dangling), builder prune (72h), and
             rmi of images used by no container (matched by image ID) older than
             --image-age-days. Never touches volumes or networks; never system prune.
             Skipped gracefully if docker is not running.

  caches     go build cache (`go clean -cache`, only if GOCACHE > 10 GiB and no
             go/compile/golangci-lint/gopls process); NuGet http-cache and temp, and
             ~/.nuget/packages versions whose .nupkg.metadata source is
             https://api.nuget.org/ or https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/dnceng/ and that are
             unused for --nuget-age-days and not among the newest --nuget-keep-versions
             (never local/file feeds; http-cache/temp clearing is skipped while a
             dotnet/MSBuild/VBCSCompiler process runs); `yarn cache clean` and
             `npm cache clean --force`; gzip in place of old, unopened pi session
             .jsonl files (never deleted); `git worktree prune` in every discovered
             repo (only drops admin entries whose directory is gone).

Suggestions (never done): dangling docker volumes, ~/.nuget/packages size, total size
of the worktrees that are kept.
"""
